From 345862c5ab0b903f50563ebe3f4ee0d7354b6f8c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Xander Burchartz <210020462+xanderburchartz@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 12:50:09 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 08/13] iOS: dialogs on small touch screens

Fit the remaining dialogs (connections, route and mark properties, route
manager, AIS target list, data monitor, about, message boxes) to a phone
screen: iOS style header with Cancel/Done, wrapped labels, wider inputs
and no fixed desktop minimum sizes. navutil: one-time iOS defaults for the
chart text size and a reset of a wrongly stored locale.

The iOS implementation lives in the iOS app layer (app/ios/*_ios.cpp in the
opencpn-ios repository); the core only declares and calls it.

All changes are inside #ifdef __OCPN__IOS__; other platforms are unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
